  "full_text": "Well, Mr. God, what do you want to do? So, Moses says, wife, the ark needs polishing. And the wife says, what, just because I'm a woman, I have to wipe the cherubs? There you go. So, Mr. God says, cherubim. The day that come after him shall be as stoned at this day as they were before the Friday. Surely such are the dwellings of the wicked, and this is the place of him that know not God. So, uh, today's a pretty good day. So, uh, how about some drumming? I don't know. Singing in the sunshine Laughing in the rain Hittin' on the moonshine, rockin' in the grain. Got no time to pack my bags, foot's outside the door. Got a day that can't be late for the hell-high hula ball. Used to sing the mountains, mountains lost the way. Now I'm singing all my songs to the girl who won my heart. She's only three years old, it's a real fine way to start. Do-wop, do-do-do-do-do-do-wop. Do-wop, do-do-do-do-do-do-wop. Do-do-do-do-do-do-wop. Do-do-do-do-do-do-do-wop. Do-do-do-do-do-do-do-wop. Tattoo, tattoo, tattoo, tattoo. Tattoo, tattoo, tattoo, tattoo.",
